# Manual interface: brings up the AR8030 kernel netdev bridge over the RF
# link (see driver/linux/net/net_dev.c). ar8030-netdev-demo assigns the IP
# itself (-P, ar_net_netif_create()'s own ifconfig call), so this is
# "manual" rather than "static" -- ifupdown would otherwise fight it over
# the address. Needs ar8030d already running and the AR8030 already
# paired; if `ifup ar_net0` hangs, it's retrying bb_host_connect/
# bb_dev_getlist in a loop waiting for either -- run ar8030-pair first.
#
# slot 0 / port 2 has to match the peer's ar8030-tun invocation exactly;
# see package/ar8030/files/etc/network/interfaces.d/tun0 in
# OpenIPC/sbc-groundstations.
iface ar_net0 inet manual
	pre-up /usr/bin/ar8030-netdev-demo -c -n ar_net0 -s 0 -p 2 -T 0 -P 192.168.100.1
	post-down /usr/bin/ar8030-netdev-demo -d -n ar_net0 -s 0 -p 2
